From b43c97454bb8b423abc9d4a706d44efb0a1ba684 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shaun Adams <s.adams@f5.com>
Date: Fri, 12 Jun 2026 15:51:55 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 17/42] transports: POST
 /api/tenants/{tenant_id}/governance/virtual-keys (admin create per-tenant VK)

Companion to the tenant-scoped provider POST: the second admin write
needed to make the inference plane end-to-end testable per tenant. The
inference VK->tenant resolver (patch 0009) reads tenant_id off the
TableVirtualKey row; this handler is what lets a platform-admin mint
that row via the API rather than directly through the DB.

Handler:
- Reads tenant_id from ctx (set by RequireTenantPathMiddleware from
  patch 0015), validates the minimum payload (name required), mints
  a governance-prefixed VK value if the caller omits one, then calls
  the existing ConfigStore.CreateVirtualKey with tenant_id pinned on
  the TableVirtualKey row.
- Best-effort cache invalidation via the same TenantRuntimeEvictor
  interface the provider handler uses, so the next inference attempt
  for this tenant resolves the freshly minted VK without waiting for
  the 60s resolver cache TTL.
- Response carries the resulting id + value so E2E (or the operator)
  can drive inference immediately without re-querying.

Scope: POST only. The legacy /api/governance/virtual-keys still serves
the rich team/customer/access-profile/budget/rate-limit/per-provider
linkage shape; those compositions can be added under the
tenant-scoped route family once AdminAuthz resolves a real
tenant-admin caller (Phase 4).

Wires into server.go under the same multi-tenant gate that mounts
the provider handler.

Ref: https://jira.f5net.com/browse/XC-25496
